The room companion libreecho-intercomd is compiled from LibreEcho-UI 0.16.8 public source, commit 984ebc22cf68f1900e931d1129357db91951ea06, copyright LibreEcho contributors. It implements the LEIC1/READY local room interface, Assist hold, room policy checks, room indication, indexed microphone stream and system PCM mixer output. See the bundled MIT licence and https://github.com/sn45k58myn-dev/LibreEcho-UI/tree/984ebc22cf68f1900e931d1129357db91951ea06.

The optional FIFO adapter was written for Echo 2 Linux with AI assistance. Both static Linux executables include the musl C library under the licensing terms distributed with the compiler target.

GCC runtime portions are distributed with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1 and the GNU General Public License 3. The original texts are included as COPYING.RUNTIME and COPYING3.
